// t-typ-mod-02: the pattern compiler's alias chase fills a typedef body's
// write-once resolution cell mid-compile, so a name a later sibling
// declares resolves to the outer definition it shadows, for every use of
// the alias.
//
// StructPatternNode::compile_int_inner (graphix-compiler/src/node/pattern.rs:436)
// expands a Ref predicate with lookup_ref until it is no Ref. For `u`, typed
// A1, the second step resolves the B in A1's BODY, a cell every expansion of
// A1 shares, in the env being compiled: the block's `type B = i64` is not
// registered yet, so TypeRef::resolve_in (graphix-types/src/typ/mod.rs:627)
// fills the cell with the outer B for good. A2, the same text in the same
// scope, is first expanded at typecheck under the full env and means the
// block's B. design/env_independent_typerefs.md: "A fill is correct iff the
// resolving env already holds the name's FINAL target"; a typedef body may
// name a later sibling (types.rs typedef_body_names_a_later_sibling).
// `let u: (A1, i64) = never()` (no destructuring, so no chase on A1) prints
// ("A1", "A2").
//
// A definition's check under its captured env (GXLambda body check and
// DefTable::record's seed_refs_seen over the def's env) fills the same way:
// replace the `let (u, n)` line with `let g = |x: i64| { let q: [A1, null] =
// never(); x };` and both arms with `[A1, null] as _` / `[A2, null] as _`
// (probe `[i64, string, null]`): ("not A1", "A2").
// File level, core prelude: `type C = Pos; let (o, n): (C, i64) = never();
// type Pos = {x: i64, y: i64}; let c: C = {x: 3, y: 4}; c.x` is refused
// ("C does not contain {x: i64, y: i64}"); with `let o: [C, null] = null` in
// place of the destructuring let it prints 3.
//
// command: graphix --no-cache design/review-2026-10-05/repro/t-typ-mod-02.gx
//          (the same with --no-fusion, GRAPHIX_PAR=force, a cold and a warm
//          image; graphix-fuzz check: AGREE, every engine gives the same answer)
//
// expected: ("A1", "A2") (A1 and A2 are one definition text in one scope, and
//           the block's own B is their final target)
// observed (HEAD c722befe, debug build): ("not A1", "A2")
type B = string;
let r = {
  type A1 = B;
  type A2 = B;
  let (u, n): (A1, i64) = never();
  type B = i64;
  let probe: [i64, string] = 1;
  let t1 = select probe { A1 as _ => "A1", _ => "not A1" };
  let t2 = select probe { A2 as _ => "A2", _ => "not A2" };
  (t1, t2)
};
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:100.ms, 0));
r
